<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch state sets price of 99.35 for Feb 2007 bond.</title>
<headline>Dutch state sets price of 99.35 for Feb 2007 bond.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch Finance Ministry's capital markets agency set an initial price of 99.35 when tap sales of the 5.75 percent bond due February 2007 reopened on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Tap sales will continue from 0700 GMT to 1500 GMT each day until further notice.</p>
<p>A total of 7.5 billion guilders of the bond was outstanding before tap sales reopened.</p>
<p>The bond was first issued in January.</p>
<p>The payment date is June 23.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
